WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.840
We have all seen horror movies where
radioactivity changes an innocent

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.940
creature into some terrible monster, a
mutant.

3
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.850
So what is a mutation, really?

4
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.180
Our features come from data encoded in
our DNA, just like a hard drive, this

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.540
data can get corrupted. That's what we
call a mutation. DNA is made up of two

6
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.400
matching strands. Each strand has a
series of four letters, and they're

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.410
matched in pairs. A mutation could mean
a change in one of the letters, or even

8
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.840
cutting both strands in two. Mutations
are happening all of the time. Most

9
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.380
mutations have no effect on a cell, but
sometimes they can cause dangerous

10
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.780
changes, like the start of a cancerous
tumor. On even rarer occasions,

11
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:53.340
mutations can actually be useful and
improve a cell. This is how genetic

12
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.250
changes happen in evolution. To fight
back against DNA breakdown, an army of

13
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:03.550
repair machinery is constantly looking
for changes in DNA and fixing it.

14
00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:10.470
How can DNA damage be repaired? Once a
mutation is found, DNA repair machinery

15
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.080
destroys the damaged part and rebuilds
it. Since DNA has two strands, there's

16
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.850
usually a backup copy that could be
used as a template. If both strands

17
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:26.240
have been broken apart, they can often
be simply reconnected. Be thankful for

18
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.260
your DNA repair machinery, as a typical
cell in your body goes through

19
00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:35.060
thousands of mutations every day.
That's several per minute per cell.

20
00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.050
Without fixing them, you wouldn't stay
healthy for very long.

